## 🎤 12. SOC Interview Questions

**Q1. What is PowerShell?**  
A command-line shell and scripting language used for administration and automation on Windows.

**Q2. What is Event ID 4104?**  
It records PowerShell script block logging information when the relevant logging is configured.

**Q3. Why is PowerShell monitored by SOC teams?**  
Because it is a legitimate administrative tool that can also be abused to perform suspicious actions.

**Q4. What is script block logging?**  
A logging feature that records information about PowerShell script blocks that are processed.

**Q5. Why correlate Event ID 4104 with Event ID 4688?**  
To compare script activity with process execution and build a more complete timeline.

**Q6. Does an encoded PowerShell command automatically mean malware?**  
No. It is a signal to investigate the command's context, source, purpose, and related behavior.

